---
/**
 * Privacy
 * URL: /privacy
 *
 * What the site does with personal data, under the GDPR (in the
 * Netherlands, the AVG). Adapted from the privacy page on the previous
 * hansmartens.dev and checked against this site's code on 2026-11-23:
 *
 *   contact form   name, email, optional subject, message; sent by email
 *                  through Resend (src/pages/api/contact.ts), not stored
 *   newsletter     email address, added to a Resend contact list only once
 *                  the subscriber clicks the link in the confirmation email
 *                  (src/pages/api/newsletter.ts)
 *   analytics      none: Analytics.astro loads Google Analytics or Tag
 *                  Manager only when PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID or
 *                  PUBLIC_GTM_ID is set. If either is ever set, this page
 *                  must say so, and the cookie section below changes too.
 *   cookies        none; the colour mode is kept in localStorage.theme (with
 *                  darkOnly in config/mode.config: nothing stored)
 *   fonts          self-hosted (@fontsource in global.css), no font CDN
 *   hosting        Vercel
 *
 * Keep it in step with the site: a policy that describes something the
 * site doesn't do is as wrong as one that leaves out something it does.
 */
import SiteLayout from '@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import SectionHead from '@/components/sections/SectionHead.astro';
import siteConfig from '@/config/site.config';

const updated = new Date('2026-11-27');
const updatedLabel = updated.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });
const mail = `mailto:${siteConfig.email}`;
import { darkOnly } from '@/config/mode.config';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What hansmartens.dev does with your personal data: the contact form, hosting, and your rights under the GDPR."
>
  <header class="shell pt-[180px] max-[800px]:pt-[130px]">
    <SectionHead
      as="h1"
      title="Privacy"
      blurb="What this website does with your personal data, and the rights you have under the GDPR."
    />
  </header>

  <section class="shell mt-16 max-[800px]:mt-10">
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-[68ch] dark:prose-invert" data-reveal-content>
      <p class="label-mono text-foreground-muted">Last updated {updatedLabel}</p>

      <p>
        This page explains what personal data this website collects, why, and what happens to it. I
        only process the data I need to answer you and to run the website, and I never sell it.
      </p>

      <h2>Who I am</h2>
      <p>
        This website is run by {siteConfig.name}, an Astro developer in {siteConfig.location}. I'm
        responsible for the personal data described on this page (the "data controller" in the
        GDPR).
      </p>
      <p>Email: <a href={mail}>{siteConfig.email}</a></p>

      <h2>The contact form</h2>
      <p>
        When you send a message with the contact form, I receive your name, your email address, the
        subject if you fill it in, and your message. The form sends it to my mailbox as an email,
        through the email service Resend. It isn't stored in a database on this website. I use it
        only to read your message and answer you.
      </p>
      <p>Legal basis: my legitimate interest in answering the messages people send me.</p>

      <h2>The newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        If you subscribe to new posts by email, I receive your email address. You first get an
        email with a link to confirm. Only when you click it is your address added to my mailing
        list, which is kept at the email service Resend. Resend also sends the newsletter. I use
        your address only to email you when a new post is published.
      </p>
      <p>You can unsubscribe at any time, with the link in every newsletter or by emailing me.</p>
      <p>Legal basis: your consent, which you give by confirming your subscription.</p>

      <h2>Email and WhatsApp</h2>
      <p>
        If you email me or send me a WhatsApp message, I receive what you send, together with your
        email address or phone number, and use it only to answer you. The WhatsApp button opens
        WhatsApp, a service of Meta, and only when you click it. Nothing from WhatsApp is loaded on
        this website before that.
      </p>

      <h2>Visits</h2>
      <p>
        This website doesn't use analytics. It doesn't count or follow visitors, and there are no
        advertising or social media trackers on it.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        This website is hosted by Vercel. Like every host, Vercel processes technical data, such as
        IP addresses and browser information, in its server logs, to deliver the website securely
        and reliably.
      </p>
      <p>Legal basis: my legitimate interest in running a secure website.</p>

      <h2>Cookies and storage</h2>
      {
        darkOnly ? (
          <p>This website sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser.</p>
        ) : (
          <p>
            This website sets no cookies. If you choose light or dark mode with the button in the
            header, your browser remembers that choice in its local storage, so the next page opens
            in the same mode. The choice stays on your device and isn't sent to me or anyone else.
            You can delete it by clearing this website's data in your browser.
          </p>
        )
      }
      <p>
        The fonts are served from this website itself, so loading a page doesn't contact a font
        service.
      </p>

      <h2>Who receives your data</h2>
      <p>I share personal data only with the services needed to run this website:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Vercel</strong>: hosting the website</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong>: delivering contact form messages, and keeping the newsletter list and sending the newsletter</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Both are based in the United States. Where data is transferred outside the European Economic
        Area, this happens under appropriate safeguards, such as the EU–US Data Privacy Framework or
        the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses. I never sell personal data or share
        it for advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
      <p>I keep messages, from the contact form, email or WhatsApp, as long as I need them to answer you.</p>
      <p>
        I keep your email address for the newsletter until you unsubscribe or ask me to delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>see the personal data I hold about you;</li>
        <li>have it corrected;</li>
        <li>have it deleted;</li>
        <li>limit or object to how I use it;</li>
        <li>receive it in a format you can take elsewhere.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To use any of these rights, email me at <a href={mail}>{siteConfig.email}</a>. You can also
        file a complaint with the Dutch Data Protection Authority, the <a
          href="https://www.autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>All traffic to this website is encrypted (HTTPS).</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        When the website or the services it uses change, I update this page. The date at the top
        shows when it was last changed.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        If something on this page is unclear, or you have a question about your data, email me at <a
          href={mail}>{siteConfig.email}</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="pb-[120px] max-[800px]:pb-[80px]"></div>
</SiteLayout>
